{# ============================================================================
   TODAY'S WATCHES ACROSS THE ORGANIZATION — the roster's cell on `/`,
   ported from the design's org.widgets.js `watches`.

   ONE ROW PER STATION ON THIS MODULE'S BOOKS, in any area: what its watch
   asks for, who is on it, and how many of them the handset bore out. The
   AREA column is the only thing this has that the area's own stations card
   does not — every figure beside it is that card's reading, unchanged.

   TWO THINGS THE DESIGN DREW THAT THIS DOES NOT. Its header row says
   "post"; the vocabulary is STATION now, and a screen shipped with the
   older word would teach it back. And it prints the workshop's own index
   chip in the tab — the drawing's referencing system, not product, as the
   dashboard this lands on says of itself.

   WHAT IT ADDS INSTEAD IS `.ao-by`. A contributed cell names its
   contributor, so the day this module is uninstalled its disappearance
   reads as the system working rather than as a bug. That mark is the host's
   vocabulary and the page links the sheet that draws it.

   BOUNDED. A dashboard card never grows with its data: the first few rows,
   the count, and the one door out.

   IT READS `by.roster` AND NOTHING ELSE. The host renders every contributed
   cell with `with_context: false` against ONE map, each contributor's own
   answers under its own slug — so a cell cannot read another module's
   numbers by accident, and the name it reads under is the slug its module
   provider declares.
   ========================================================================= #}
{% set roster = by[constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Org\\RosterOrgOverview::SLUG')] %}
<div class="c" data-w="watches">
    <span class="tab">Today&rsquo;s watches<span class="src">&middot;
        <time datetime="{{ roster.day.format('Y-m-d') }}" data-localtime-format="day">{{ roster.day.format('D j M')|lower }}</time>
        &middot; {{ roster.onTheWatch }} on the watch now
        {%- if roster.short %} &middot; <span class="r">{{ roster.short }} short</span>{% endif %}</span></span>

    {% if roster.watches|length > roster.shown %}
        <a class="more" href="{{ roster.rosterUrl }}">{{ roster.shown }} of {{ roster.watches|length }} &middot; the roster &rarr;</a>
    {% else %}
        <a class="more" href="{{ roster.rosterUrl }}">The roster &rarr;</a>
    {% endif %}

    <span class="ao-by"><i></i>roster</span>

    {% if roster.watches is empty %}
        <p class="zeb">No station is on the roster&rsquo;s books in any area yet. A watch is given to a station deliberately, so none is assumed &mdash; and until one is, this module counts nothing and reports on nobody.</p>
    {% else %}
        <table class="tbl">
            <tr>
                <th>station</th>
                <th>area</th>
                <th>the watch</th>
                <th>on it now</th>
                <th>verified</th>
            </tr>
            {% for row in roster.watches|slice(0, roster.shown) %}
                <tr>
                    <td{{ row.standsAWatch ? '' : ' class="fog"' }}>
                        {%- if row.standsAWatch %}<b>{{ row.stationName }}</b>{% else %}{{ row.stationName }}{% endif %}
                        <span class="mono">{{ row.stationCode ?: '—' }}</span>
                    </td>
                    <td{{ row.standsAWatch ? '' : ' class="fog"' }}>{{ row.areaName }}</td>
                    <td{{ row.standsAWatch ? '' : ' class="fog"' }}>{{ row.watch }}</td>
                    <td{{ row.standsAWatch ? '' : ' class="fog"' }}>{{ row.onItNow }}</td>
                    {# A STATION THAT STANDS NO WATCH HAS NOTHING TO VERIFY, so
                       the column says how it reads instead of printing 0 of 0 —
                       null and zero are different facts. #}
                    <td class="{{ row.tone }}">
                        {%- if row.standsAWatch -%}
                            {{ row.verified }} of {{ row.onItNow }}
                        {%- else -%}
                            {{ row.state.label|lower }}
                            {%- if row.silentFor is not null %} &middot; {{ row.silentFor }} min{% endif -%}
                        {%- endif -%}
                    </td>
                </tr>
            {% endfor %}
        </table>
    {% endif %}
</div>
